equation of the curve is $r=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/f8/f85ddaa01b6f2232627375ec622232a245c6e7e21fb9e294cd0801fd45433d73.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543508 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ad4cf0e-4346-5277-9026-122b5ae58f25" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Polar Equation of a Circle Given a Point on the Circumference"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02678531-9c49-5d43-ac23-ff708b70c36a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542643} {:answer/id #uuid "61ecb54f-4cf4-55d8-87f1-9831a5a2ebfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542908} {:answer/id #uuid "998509c8-dbe2-5773-9816-4eebd147b0d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543041} {:answer/id #uuid "cf7c9130-467b-5bbc-adb8-bda779f897f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543176} {:answer/id #uuid "f056c49a-e227-56b9-82af-8dff44909eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf7c9130-467b-5bbc-adb8-bda779f897f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543176} :answer-field/id #uuid "73fea5df-076e-5c43-b1fe-9e9657547c19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5fff1012-20ae-54c4-8327-06d77bbed9eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-121522" :question/problem "The polar curve $r=k\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ where $k$ is a constant, passes through the point $A$ with Cartesian coordinates $(-\\frac{9}{2},-\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}).$ What is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the polar coordinates of the point $A.$ The distance from $A$ to the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}+{(-\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{81}{4}+\\frac{27}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{27} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $A$ lies in the third quadrant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta  & =\\pi +\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}| \\\\  & =\\pi +\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{-\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}}{-\\frac{9}{2}}| \\\\  & =\\pi +\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the polar coordinates of $A$ are $(r,\\theta )=(3\\sqrt{3},\\frac{7\\pi }{6}).$  \n\nTo find the value of $k$, we substitute the polar coordinates of the point $A$ into the polar equation of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =k\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 3\\sqrt{3} & =k\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{6}) \\\\ 3\\sqrt{3} & =k(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\ k & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equation of the curve is $r=-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/99/999a34650676174083aa479669eecca0c837dc8e5f1397a81a8949d8f9dc9de1.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106070 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3504bc1-05d2-55c5-b862-84be2e2516f7" :knowledge-point/title "The Polar Equation of a Circle Centered on the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95f16191-954d-5643-9248-20476e9329a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/06/06c99a85fb7d6b56241d0f574424a47397698dc1bb0b9d15d6ba49637126fc8b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102307} {:answer/id #uuid "ac33cadd-3317-5a8b-bff1-ee122245f136" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/16/1641aad508d38da90e1df72f98131faffb0cdbc19ee43abc946b47a86f800586.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102308} {:answer/id #uuid "bd310d16-0f42-527a-970e-972cbcb2e1ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/05/05996c6895718404008ed930e4410d7f410f946568721b06736bd7915afa88ba.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102309} {:answer/id #uuid "d0579e02-5f8e-5de8-aad3-67d38a2e66cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/dc/dc198a4464f8e0a9bc78907bf199acbce3bd4f61baf089739eed8497bfd0d22e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102310} {:answer/id #uuid "dda4921d-0d6c-577b-8e75-9b878d7aa0ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/50/50e39385446350d0abbe49e6a8b5ce1118d68ac107202e141d3f402d0af9f1a6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd310d16-0f42-527a-970e-972cbcb2e1ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/05/05996c6895718404008ed930e4410d7f410f946568721b06736bd7915afa88ba.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102309} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b8adf58-e724-5f06-bbec-858357f92f9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102306}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ea96cdbb-5bc6-555b-973f-b15da8fc1288" :question/math-academy-id "q-16469" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of the polar curve $r=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ?$" :question/worked-solution "The polar equation $r=2a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ defines a circle of radius $|a|$ centered at the point $(a,0).$\n\nIn our case, we have $r=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ and therefore\n\n$$\na=\\frac{4}{2}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $r=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ gives a circle of radius $|2|=2$ centered at the point $(2,0),$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/05/05996c6895718404008ed930e4410d7f410f946568721b06736bd7915afa88ba.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543521 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105759 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22b3da96-2573-513e-ae70-2b49510acd87" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Polar Equation of a Circle Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26170fed-0808-5028-b332-6f767e823106" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=4\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542737} {:answer/id #uuid "8306e858-4a13-52c8-b0b3-d9a21b955da0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=2\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542989} {:answer/id #uuid "c9e39e06-98ba-5d78-b2ed-a3a2bc1bd3ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543166} {:answer/id #uuid "db805938-1a26-554c-8de2-fa5d15082599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543201} {:answer/id #uuid "f5748e38-7810-59d4-bbef-a5e6fa736e65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543268}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5748e38-7810-59d4-bbef-a5e6fa736e65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543268} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed1dad79-818d-5104-8482-8cae5910311a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543462}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7fdddd6d-d41d-5369-b195-6ee0cc2418de" :question/math-academy-id "q-16470" :question/problem "![](images/ae/aee2a6a03d8dc10cd56e6e2df279fcf88672d0c83d0ae7abc86a0c8b1a3e434d.png)\n\nWhat is the polar equation of the curve shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows a circle of radius $a=1$ centered at the point $(0,1).$ \n\nIn polar coordinates, the equation of such a circle is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =2a\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543486 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3504bc1-05d2-55c5-b862-84be2e2516f7" :knowledge-point/title "The Polar Equation of a Circle Centered on the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1160f38c-bfa8-5ecd-b8c4-38d9798b8df5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e7/e71470925044353f9dae67f7720e8ace6672a06f0ca1c70d26d256005a9f5712.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542681} {:answer/id #uuid "5fe84bfa-6f9a-52de-ae68-c99ebec95c69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/dc/dc5ba4e04995cfc70ed35b8662322fd169bc2b9ab88b6d85f24847e93f6f33af.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542899} {:answer/id #uuid "ba6b781d-f4d7-5f13-9d93-2848afdf07c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0c/0cdff41c64c8c0600d1d792d5bf9c06b1aaa3511be70d2178071406f1462a3cc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543129} {:answer/id #uuid "cd3f3f92-9bd6-5d89-ae3b-b4218dd8b92d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c9