rname{sin}⁡\\theta ?$" :question/worked-solution "The polar equation $r=2a\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ defines a circle of radius $|a|$ centered at the point $(0,a).$\n\nIn our case, we have $r=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ and therefore\n\n$$\na=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $r=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ gives a circle of radius $|\\frac{5}{2}|=\\frac{5}{2}$ centered at the point $(0,2.5),$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/83/8375e6709a6a7f34183b821411aaa251341666f948164d498b012f07af744a45.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543581 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105759 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22b3da96-2573-513e-ae70-2b49510acd87" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Polar Equation of a Circle Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40c7ee0c-a229-553d-8145-37422e8684fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=-6\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542816} {:answer/id #uuid "5dc4140c-ff98-5ca1-9dfe-07b84f312647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542892} {:answer/id #uuid "7cbcd85f-3ddc-53d4-a644-eeb257393505" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542975} {:answer/id #uuid "eb7be00e-68c2-5e0d-baee-30814e8f0558" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543234} {:answer/id #uuid "f54be357-0b0e-5eb1-9cf5-f059be49aadf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f54be357-0b0e-5eb1-9cf5-f059be49aadf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543267} :answer-field/id #uuid "abd7fc75-76ad-538d-8473-a58530f6d817" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543415}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eb541cd2-06d9-513e-814b-43ef4f1b8af7" :question/math-academy-id "q-17269" :question/problem "![](images/73/7341b6d76c74c20596b627167ee90bed0f00cc435b3d1a23c7b9976e353f79d5.png)\n\nWhat is the polar equation of the curve shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows a circle of radius $|a|=|-3|=3$ centered at the point $(-3,0).$ \n\nIn polar coordinates, the equation of such a circle is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =2a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-3)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543474 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105759 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22b3da96-2573-513e-ae70-2b49510acd87" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Polar Equation of a Circle Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ead7495-9d1a-5f6e-99a3-8e36672e478a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542672} {:answer/id #uuid "39303a4a-5088-510c-9caa-10c1d8540af2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542791} {:answer/id #uuid "56848177-37b1-52a1-84d2-395faabcf2f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542876} {:answer/id #uuid "86f098f5-e383-5c34-807c-21780f62cae